OL,3,GNEWSAFire safety work still pending    
OL,4,Athree years on                         
OL,6,FA Southern Housing (SH) tenant says he 
OL,7,Fcontinues to have sleepless nights     
OL,8,Fthree years after a fire report        
OL,9,Fidentified multiple risks at his block 
OL,10,Fof flats.                              
OL,12,FMalcolm Preston, who lives at Humphreys
OL,13,FHouse in Shoreham-by-Sea, said there   
OL,14,Fhad been "no communication" about when 
OL,15,Fhigh-risk cladding identified in 2023  
OL,16,Fwould be replaced.                     
OL,18,FA BBC investigation has found almost   
OL,19,Ftwo-thirds (66%) of residential        
OL,20,Fbuildings identified as having unsafe  
OL,21,Fcladding across Kent, Sussex and Surrey
OL,22,Fhave not yet completed remedial work.  
